Z||000000||ChadMan||07-16-2001||09:16 AM||||Came out this morning to find a nice big scuff on the side of my Fiero where some sonofabitch ran into it while backing out of the spot next to mine.  I haven't seen my neighbor's car yet, but if his front bumper is scuffed with Medium Red Metallic Fiero paint, well, he'd better have made his peace with Vishnu.<P>It is phucking useless to try to keep a car nice while living in an apartment complex.  I hate scum people and wish they'd all drop dead.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||07-16-2001||10:10 AM||||I feel your pain- I live in a college dorm- and drunk college kids are probably worse drivers than your neighbor. I never brought my Fiero to school- and the week that I had to, I parked it way out and covered it with a car cover 24/7. People thought it was kinda weird, but hey, no one messed with it. The car I did drive every day got a new scuff or door chip at least every week.  Now that I'm at an apartment at home, I rented a garage to protect my baby  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||07-16-2001||10:13 AM||||are you sure maybe it didnt happen somewhere else and you didnt notice it till this morning?<P> if it happened at your apt complex then it could have been someone who was just visiting last night - pizza delivery or someone who wont be back tonight.<P> same thing happened a few years back to a guys Firebird in the apts I was living in - the guy was a real bonehead about it, was going through the parking lot looking at everyones car to see 'Who Dunnit' - and he was kinda ranting and raving at the time - like we were all guilty or suspects until he found the car with his paint on it - made a real a$$ out of himself and managed to PO everyone else at the complex<P>  in the end I dont know if he ever found out who dinged his Firebird. But for a few bucks worth the paint he totally destroyed about 100 peoples opinion of him.||||reg||11
Z||000003||Formula88||07-16-2001||10:30 AM||||I feel you pain, man.  My Grand Am got a collection of dings at the parking lot at work, and that was even after I started parking on the far side of the lot with no cars around.  I still think it was the groundkeeps with the big blowers on the back walking beside the car and hitting it with the blower when they turn their back.  Can't prove it, of course, but the dings are just in the wrong place for a car to have done it.||||reg||8
Z||000004||ChadMan||07-16-2001||10:35 AM||||Thanks for the sympathy, Lisa & Formula88.<P>I parked the car Friday night and handwashed it, so I know it had not been hit at that time.  It sat all weekend, and when I went out this morning, it had been hit.  So it had to be someone using my neighbor's spot.  If it wasn't him (and I sincerely hope it wasn't), I'll never know who it was.<P>Ken, why do you think the Firebird owner was a "bonehead" for trying to find out what spineless piece of $hit ran into his car?<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 07-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Urchin||07-16-2001||11:21 AM||||I have been fortunate enough not to have my fiero scuffed, but I recently got a new cavalier Z24, and in the 2 1/2 months I've had it, it has been dinged three times now.  And of course I can't do a damn thing about it.  Talk about tick you off!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lowered_blackgtthis_one.jpg"> <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
